              full WinUI Release build of the solution succeeds — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), optionally <Name>.Source.cs (data feed — none needed here), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (the UI-thread-free state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's idealized
  "NotFoundPage.xaml + NotFoundPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/System" is mapped onto these real
  conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("NotFound", the
  RouteTable catch-all). Same mapping the sibling system pages use (see windows-page-system-CommandHistoryPage.log).
- Namespace: TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.SystemOps (NOT ".System" — a sibling namespace segment literally named
  "System" shadows global::System for every inline System.* name, which breaks the app compile; "SystemOps"
  mirrors the route's RouteGroup.SystemOps and is collision-free — the same decision the CommandHistory unit made).
- Data sources: NONE (manifest declares no API data sources — the page renders from the unmatched route path /
  local state). The view performs no HTTP. The unmatched path is read from the live RouteMatch
  (_viewModel.Current.MatchedPath, the native location.pathname) at registration time and passed to the page.
- Suggestion engine: web/src/lib/closestRoute.ts (closestRoutes + two-row Levenshtein) is ported verbatim into
  RouteSuggestionEngine (Closest / Levenshtein / Normalize / DisplayPath). It ranks the live RouteTable.All by the
  minimum edit distance to BOTH the route path and label (lower-cased, separators stripped), keeps candidates
  within the web's distance<=6 ceiling, dedupes by route name (canonical first), and returns the web's 5-cap
  ordered by distance then ordinal path. Parameterized routes (the native analogue of the web registry's hidden
  entries), redirects and the catch-all are excluded as non-navigable. Verified headlessly against the real table
  (/vehiclees -> Vehicles at distance 1) and with controlled fixtures (ranking / ceiling / cap / tie-break / dedupe).
- Escape hatches map onto the native shell: "Go back" -> GoBack() (web window.history.back()), "Go to dashboard"
  -> NavigateTo("") index (web navigate('/')), "Open command palette" -> SearchBox.Focus() (the W3 command/search
  surface; web dispatchEvent('toggle-command-palette')), suggestion links -> NavigateTo(s.path) (web Link to). The
  view holds no router — each leaves through the surface's GoBackRequested / GoHomeRequested / OpenSearchRequested /
  NavigationRequested events, wired in ShellWindow. The web mount-time console.warn('[404]', path) is ported as the
  one-shot NotFoundDiagnostics.RecordShown(path) emitted on Loaded.
- All 7 i18n keys already exist verbatim in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (translation.notFound.*); the surface
  resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names (no new catalog rows required). The body uses
  the catalog's {0} slot filled with the display path exactly as the web fills {{path}}.
- No stubs, no TODO/FIXME, no "Coming soon", no NotImplementedException (ADR-011); placeholder scan clean (0).

